我讨厌这样。

1672
01:11:40.680 --> 01:11:44.620
I can't tell you how much leftover guacamole I've ended up eating over the years.
我没法告诉你这些年来我最后吃了多少剩下的鳄梨酱。

1673
01:11:44.840 --> 01:11:47.280
I don't even know why I make it in such great quantities.
我甚至不知道我为什么要准备那么多。

1674
01:11:47.880 --> 01:11:50.920
And then he says, listen, just sit there and pretend to cry, right?
然后他说，听着，就坐在那儿假装哭，好吗？

1675
01:11:51.060 --> 01:11:51.680
Can you do that?
你能做到吗？

1676
01:11:51.820 --> 01:11:51.920
Yeah.
能。

1677
01:11:51.920 --> 01:11:55.120
And then they both end up laughing, and it's a really sweet moment.
然后他们俩最后都笑了，那真是一个非常温馨的时刻。

1678
01:11:55.340 --> 01:11:56.180
It really is.
确实是。

1679
01:11:56.340 --> 01:12:04.960
And we got a bunch of people writing in to ask if that laugh after Kelly fake cries, if that was like a fake laugh or if Mindy broke.
我们收到很多人来信问，凯莉假哭之后的那个笑，是假笑还是明迪笑场了。

1680
01:12:05.360 --> 01:12:07.060
No, that was scripted.
不，那是剧本写的。

1681
01:12:07.200 --> 01:12:10.500
It's scripted that her fake crying made them laugh.
剧本就是写她假哭把他们逗笑了。

1682
01:12:10.700 --> 01:12:11.860
Well, I'll say this.
嗯，我得说。

1683
01:12:11.940 --> 01:12:20.340
In re-watching this episode, like three times, right, before today, I could hear Mindy's fake laugh and then her real laugh.
在重看这一集的时候，大概看了三遍吧，在今天之前，我能听到明迪的假笑，然后是她的真笑。

1684
01:12:20.460 --> 01:12:20.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1685
01:12:20.780 --> 01:12:28.880
So if you watch it, she fake cries, she fake laughs, then Steve laughs as Michael, and then Mindy laughs as herself.
所以如果你仔细看，她假哭，她假笑，然后史蒂夫作为迈克尔笑了，接着明迪作为她自己笑了。

1686
01:12:29.060 --> 01:12:29.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1687
01:12:29.420 --> 01:12:31.280
Her real laugh definitely comes out.
她的真笑绝对流露出来了。

1688
01:12:31.460 --> 01:12:31.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1689
01:12:31.800 --> 01:12:39.180
So now we're at this scene at Corporate, which we talked about a lot with Stephen, this scene where Alex comes to Pam's work.
现在我们到了公司总部的那场戏，我们和斯蒂芬聊过很多，就是亚历克斯来帕姆工作的地方那场戏。

1690
01:12:39.280 --> 01:12:42.260
He's going to kidnap her, wants to see this art.
他要带走她，想看这些艺术品。

1691
01:12:42.420 --> 01:12:44.540
He said wine and cheese, okay?
他说有红酒和奶酪，好吗？

1692
01:12:45.180 --> 01:12:46.480
That's all you got to hear.
你只需要听到这个就够了。

1693
01:12:46.920 --> 01:12:47.400
Midday.
大中午的。

1694
01:12:47.400 --> 01:12:50.400
Midday, there's an exhibit with wine and cheese.
大中午的，有个带红酒和奶酪的展览。

1695
01:12:50.600 --> 01:12:51.880
That's not being friends.
那可不是朋友之间该做的。

1696
01:12:52.360 --> 01:12:52.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1697
01:12:53.040 --> 01:12:58.820
Well, thanks to James-a-pedia, I saw all of the candy bag for this.
多亏了“詹姆斯百科”，我看到了这场戏所有的备选片段。

1698
01:12:59.200 --> 01:13:00.580
How many were there?
有多少个？

1699
01:13:00.740 --> 01:13:01.100
Ten.
十个。

1700
01:13:01.340 --> 01:13:03.040
Ten alts for this scene.
这场戏有十个备选方案。

1701
01:13:03.100 --> 01:13:03.380
Yes.
是的。

1702
01:13:03.680 --> 01:13:04.720
Oh, my word.
天哪。

1703
01:13:04.840 --> 01:13:04.980
Yeah.
是啊。

1704
01:13:04.980 --> 01:13:09.300
I wanted to count because we kind of talked about it, and it was ten.
我想数一下，因为我们之前聊过，大概有十个。

1705
01:13:09.480 --> 01:13:14.580
Ten alternate scenes, and I swear we shot so many, so many versions of it.
十个备选场景，我发誓我们拍了好多好多版本。

1706
01:13:14.700 --> 01:13:17.060
And I remember doing these scenes with Rich.
我记得和里奇一起拍这些戏份的时候。

1707
01:13:17.160 --> 01:13:18.840
It was so grueling.
真是太折磨人了。

1708
01:13:18.940 --> 01:13:20.420
And we really bonded.
我们真的建立了深厚的友谊。

1709
01:13:20.760 --> 01:13:26.980
Like, Rich and I are great friends today, I think, because we went through this moment together.
我觉得里奇和我现在能成为好朋友，就是因为我们一起经历了那个时刻。

1710
01:13:26.980 --> 01:13:29.620
Yeah, you were in the trenches of trying to find this scene.
没错，你们当时就像在战壕里一样，努力寻找这场戏的感觉。

1711
01:13:29.780 --> 01:13:30.020
Yes.
是的。

1712
01:13:30.220 --> 01:13:32.320
Well, we should have Rich on and talk about it.
嗯，我们应该请里奇来聊聊这件事。

1713
01:13:32.420 --> 01:13:33.820
We need to hear his side of things.
我们需要听听他的说法。

1714
01:13:33.940 --> 01:13:34.220
We do.
确实。

1715
01:13:34.300 --> 01:13:35.480
Of shooting this crazy scene.
关于拍摄这场疯狂戏份的经历。

1716
01:13:35.640 --> 01:13:36.160
Let's call him.
我们给他打个电话吧。

1717
01:13:36.240 --> 01:13:36.800
Rich, come on.
里奇，快来。

1718
01:13:37.260 --> 01:13:41.820
So, I feel like we really covered this, but we did have a fan write in, and I'm so sorry
我觉得我们已经聊得很透彻了，但有位粉丝写信来问，我很抱歉，

1719
01:13:41.820 --> 01:13:44.900
I didn't write down your name because I thought this was a really good observation.
我没记下你的名字，因为我觉得这是一个非常好的观察。

1720
01:13:45.340 --> 01:13:51.740
They were saying, wasn't Pam's art program three months long, and she went at the beginning
他们说，帕姆的艺术课程不是只有三个月吗，而且她是夏天刚开始的时候去的，

1721
01:13:51.740 --> 01:13:52.340
of the summer?
对吧？

1722
01:13:52.700 --> 01:13:56.660
How was she there for Halloween, and how is she still there?
那她怎么会在万圣节还在那儿，而且现在怎么还在那儿？

1723
01:13:56.980 --> 01:13:58.340
Isn't it November now?
现在不是已经十一月了吗？

1724
01:13:58.780 --> 01:14:00.220
Art school is a mystery.
艺术学校真是个谜。

1725
01:14:00.960 --> 01:14:01.880
It's a mystery.
确实是个谜。

1726
01:14:02.240 --> 01:14:02.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1727
01:14:02.860 --> 01:14:03.060
Yeah.
没错。

1728
01:14:03.420 --> 01:14:04.640
That's a good catch.
这观察力真敏锐。

1729
01:14:04.860 --> 01:14:06.660
I still want to know if she has parking.
我还是想知道她有没有停车位。

1730
01:14:07.040 --> 01:14:09.520
You know, these are things we're going to wonder about art school.
你知道，这些都是我们会对艺术学校产生好奇的地方。

1731
01:14:09.600 --> 01:14:14.100
Well, she's having to go into Manhattan for her corporate job because Pratt's out in Brooklyn.
嗯，她得去曼哈顿做她的企业工作，因为普拉特学院在布鲁克林。

1732
01:14:14.340 --> 01:14:14.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1733
01:14:16.280 --> 01:14:19.080
Well, we end this episode with Andy, Angela, and Dwight.
这一集的结尾是安迪、安吉拉和德怀特。

1734
01:14:19.240 --> 01:14:19.580
Yeah.
没错。

1735
01:14:19.720 --> 01:14:23.540
Because Andy has found the perfect place for them to get married, and it's Shrute FarMs.
因为安迪为他们找到了完美的结婚地点，就是施鲁特农场。

1736
01:14:23.700 --> 01:14:25.240
It ticks all of the boxes.
它满足了所有条件。

1737
01:14:25.240 --> 01:14:29.320
Angela gave them a list of what the wedding location had to include.
安吉拉给了他们一份婚礼场地必须具备的清单。

1738
01:14:29.880 --> 01:14:30.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1739
01:14:30.320 --> 01:14:33.780
And Dwight tells them he thinks they should have the Excalibur package.
德怀特告诉他们，他觉得他们应该选择“石中剑”套餐。

1740
01:14:34.200 --> 01:14:35.940
It's going to have everything they need.
那里面会有他们需要的一切。

1741
01:14:36.400 --> 01:14:38.740
Angela is clearly delighted.
安吉拉显然很高兴。

1742
01:14:39.200 --> 01:14:40.440
Andy is relieved.
安迪如释重负。

1743
01:14:40.660 --> 01:14:47.140
And Jenna, all I could think of when I watched the scene was Jim and Pam planned Pam's wedding
珍娜，我看这场戏时唯一能想到的就是，吉姆和帕姆曾帮帕姆筹划过她和罗伊的婚礼，

1744
01:14:47.140 --> 01:14:51.620
to Roy, and now Angela and Dwight are going to plan her wedding to Andy.
而现在安吉拉和德怀特要帮她筹划她和安迪的婚礼。

1745
01:14:51.620 --> 01:14:53.080
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1746
01:14:53.820 --> 01:14:54.480
Right?
对吧？

1747
01:14:54.820 --> 01:14:55.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1748
01:14:55.720 --> 01:14:56.900
It's sort of a callback.
这算是一种呼应吧。

1749
01:14:56.900 --> 01:14:57.940
It is.
确实是。

1750
01:14:58.420 --> 01:15:02.320
You know, there's another little weird callback in this scene.
你知道，这场戏里还有另一个奇怪的小呼应。

1751
01:15:02.600 --> 01:15:09.420
A lot of people wrote in with this fan catch that the funeral homes director in Job Fair.
很多人写信提到这个粉丝发现，在《招聘会》那一集中，殡仪馆馆长也在场。

1752
01:15:09.560 --> 01:15:09.940
Yes.
是的。

1753
01:15:10.060 --> 01:15:10.980
He's in the album.
他在相册里。

1754
01:15:11.220 --> 01:15:12.140
He's in the album.
他在相册里。

1755
01:15:12.260 --> 01:15:13.900
He got married at Shrute FarMs.
他在施鲁特农场结的婚。

1756
01:15:13.980 --> 01:15:14.360
Yes.
是的。

1757
01:15:14.360 --> 01:15:18.880
Well, Lester said in his interview that they loved this guy, and they used him twice,
莱斯特在采访中说他们很喜欢这个人，所以用了他两次，

1758
01:15:18.920 --> 01:15:22.960
and they also thought it worked because the Shrutes get married in their own graves.
而且他们认为这很合理，因为施鲁特家族的人就是在自己的坟墓里结婚的。

1759
01:15:23.200 --> 01:15:23.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1760
01:15:23.580 --> 01:15:26.540
So he felt that he would know about Shrute FarMs.
所以他觉得那个人应该了解施鲁特农场。

1761
01:15:26.920 --> 01:15:27.200
Yeah.
没错。

1762
01:15:27.520 --> 01:15:28.580
That's a great catch.
真是个了不起的发现。

1763
01:15:30.020 --> 01:15:32.460
Well, all righty, Dwighty.
好吧，德怀特。

1764
01:15:32.460 --> 01:15:34.580
That was customer survey.
那是《客户调查》那一集。

1765
01:15:35.000 --> 01:15:38.000
Thank you so much, James Carey, for sending me those scripts.
非常感谢詹姆斯·凯里寄给我的那些剧本。

1766
01:15:38.260 --> 01:15:43.200
I also got in touch with Randy Cordray on this one because I couldn't remember if the
我还就这件事联系了兰迪·科德雷，因为我不记得

1767
01:15:43.200 --> 01:15:44.420
Bluetooths were real.
蓝牙耳机是不是真的了。

1768
01:15:44.640 --> 01:15:46.040
I was so convinced.
我当时深信不疑。

1769
01:15:46.220 --> 01:15:49.440
So I wrote Randy, and I was like, they weren't real, right?
所以我写信给兰迪，问他：它们不是真的，对吧？

1770
01:15:49.440 --> 01:15:50.560
No, they weren't real.
不，它们不是真的。

1771
01:15:50.560 --> 01:15:53.040
They talked about it quite a bit on the DVD commentary.
他们在DVD评论音轨里聊过不少次。

1772
01:15:53.420 --> 01:15:57.900
And of course, a humongous thank you to Stephen Merchant.
当然，还要向斯蒂芬·莫昌特表示万分感谢。

1773
01:15:58.540 --> 01:15:59.320
We love you.
我们爱你。

1774
01:15:59.540 --> 01:16:00.220
We love you.
我们爱你。

1775
01:16:00.400 --> 01:16:01.400
Please come back.
请再回来吧。

1776
01:16:01.400 --> 01:16:01.980
Yes.
好的。

1777
01:16:02.460 --> 01:16:04.300
And next week, we have Business Trip.
下周我们要聊《出差》那一集。

1778
01:16:04.540 --> 01:16:06.100
Michael's going to Canada, y'all.
迈克尔要去加拿大了，各位。

1779
01:16:06.280 --> 01:16:07.680
And Rich, we're going to call you.
还有里奇，我们会给你打电话的。

1780
01:16:07.980 --> 01:16:08.380
Yes.
好的。

1781
01:16:08.500 --> 01:16:13.860
Rich, you will be in Business Trip, an episode that your character does not appear.
里奇，你会出现在《出差》这一集里，尽管你的角色并没有在剧中露面。

1782
01:16:14.020 --> 01:16:15.640
But we have questions for you.
但我们有一些问题要问你。

1783
01:16:15.700 --> 01:16:16.220
We do.
没错。

1784
01:16:16.240 --> 01:16:18.180
And this is our podcast, so we can do that.
这是我们的播客，所以我们可以这么做。

1785
01:16:18.280 --> 01:16:18.760
That's right.
说得对。

1786
01:16:19.200 --> 01:16:20.100
All righty, Dwighty.
好吧，德怀特。

1787
01:16:20.200 --> 01:16:21.280
You guys have a good week.
祝大家这周过得愉快。

1788
01:16:21.460 --> 01:16:23.100
You are really loving that phrase.
你真的很喜欢那个短语。

1789
01:16:23.340 --> 01:16:24.900
I said it one time too many, didn't I?
我说了太多次了，对吧？

1790
01:16:25.020 --> 01:16:29.060
Maybe, but I like that when you attach to something, you go for it.
也许吧，但我喜欢你一旦认准了什么，就会坚持到底的劲头。

1791
01:16:29.160 --> 01:16:29.520
Thank you.
谢谢。

1792
01:16:29.760 --> 01:16:30.240
All right.
好的。

1793
01:16:30.240 --> 01:16:31.740
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1794
01:16:31.840 --> 01:16:33.080
That was your extra long goodbye.
那是你超长的告别。

